# Salesforce Deployment Rules

## Proactive deploy (default)

When a task changes Salesforce metadata (including **LWC** bundles), **run the targeted deploy** before wrapping up the same turn — but **only after** the user has approved implementation per **Confirm Before Implement** (`diagnose-before-fix.mdc`). Do not deploy exploratory or unapproved changes.

**Skip or defer** if the user asked to keep changes local, not deploy yet, or treat the work as draft; if implementation was not yet approved; or if a deploy is impossible in context (e.g. no CLI org).

### Scope: only what you edited (since last deploy)

Deploy **only** metadata paths **you edited in the current task** since the **last successful org deploy** in this session—not every bundle that “relates” to the feature, not a repo-wide grep fan-out, and never all of `force-app`.

- Track the set of changed paths (LWC bundle folders, static resources, Apex classes, etc.) as you work.
- When it is time to deploy, use **one** `sf project deploy start` with **multiple `--source-dir` flags**—one per changed path—so the org gets a single bundled deploy.
- Do **not** redeploy bundles that were already deployed unchanged earlier in the session.
- Exception: atomic rollback split (schema-only deploy, then Apex with tests) still uses **two** deploy calls when required—each call still lists only the paths that changed in that step.

