Run deploys only from `FIMBY/` where `sfdx-project.json` exists, using exactly:
`sf project deploy start --source-dir "<path>" --wait 10 2>&1 | Select-Object -Last 20`

Use `working_directory: c:\Users\srathjen\FIMBY\FIMBY`

Do not use `cd`, `Set-Location`, `&&`, or other shell navigation in the command. Do not include `--target-org`. Keep `| Select-Object -Last 20`.

For LWCs, `--source-dir` must point to the bundle folder, not an individual file. Repeat `--source-dir` for each edited bundle in the same deploy command.

### MANDATORY pre-deploy check — run this mental checklist EVERY deploy

1. **Does `--source-dir` include ANY `.cls` or `.trigger` file?**
   - YES → you MUST add `--tests TestClassName` for each relevant test class. Omitting `--tests` causes the org to run ALL tests (~600), which wastes 20+ minutes and must be cancelled.
   - NO (LWC, objects, layouts, flows, etc. only) → do NOT include `--tests` or `--test-level`.
2. Never use `--test-level RunAllTestsInOrg` or `--test-level RunLocalTests` — always name specific tests.
3. Confirm each test class still covers the Apex change (target 80%+, 75%+ only in a pinch).

### MANDATORY pre-deploy Code Analyzer gate

Run this before **every** deploy that includes Apex or LWC, after tests are chosen and before `sf project deploy start`.

1. Scan exactly the deployed paths (same set as `--source-dir`, including each test class), using `working_directory: c:\Users\srathjen\FIMBY` (repo root) so `code-analyzer.yml` applies:
   `sf code-analyzer run --target "FIMBY/force-app/main/default/classes/MyClass.cls" --target "FIMBY/force-app/main/default/lwc/myBundle" --output-file "C:\Users\srathjen\AppData\Local\Temp\ca-predeploy.csv" 2>&1 | Select-Object -Last 3`
   Then list blockers:
   `Import-Csv "C:\Users\srathjen\AppData\Local\Temp\ca-predeploy.csv" | Where-Object { [int]$_.severity -le 2 } | ForEach-Object { "{0} | {1}:{2} | {3}" -f $_.severity, (Split-Path $_.file -Leaf), $_.startLine, $_.rule }`
2. **Any Critical (1) or High (2) finding anywhere in a deployed file blocks the deploy**, including pre-existing findings on lines you didn't change. Fix them, re-scan to zero, and make sure the named tests still cover the class. Fixes must be behaviour-neutral or covered by tests; follow `fimby-apex-patterns.mdc` → *Code Analyzer hygiene* (for example, explicit `WITH SYSTEM_MODE` / `as system` on authorization helpers).
   - If a finding can't be fixed safely within the task (it needs a design change, or user mode would break community access), **stop and ask Stephen** before deploying. Never suppress it to get past the gate.
   - Expect the first deploy of a large legacy file to carry extra work (e.g. `FimbyConversationController` had ~37 CRUD findings). Mention that scope in the plan before starting.
3. Moderate (3) on lines you changed: fix when cheap, otherwise list in the summary. Low/Info: no action required.
4. **Editor mirror:** if `c:\Users\srathjen\FIMBY\.ai\problems\all-problems.json` has a `generatedAt` within the last ~15 minutes, read it too and treat `Sev1`/`Sev2` entries for deployed files the same way. It only covers files Stephen has scanned in the editor, so the CLI scan above remains the gate.
5. In the deploy summary, add one line: `Code Analyzer: 0 Critical/High in N deployed files (fixed X pre-existing)`.

If deploy output ends with `Error (MetadataTransferError): Metadata API request failed: Missing message metadata.transfer:Finalizing for locale en_US.` then the deployment succeeded. This is a known Salesforce CLI locale bug that also corrupts the test summary — the pass/fail counts, percentages, and the `Failed: ×` indicator are all display artifacts and do not reflect actual test results. Treat the deploy as fully successful. Do not run `sf project deploy report` to re-check.

### Post-deploy: Publish Experience Cloud after LWC deploys

After a **successful** LWC deploy, immediately publish the Experience Cloud site so changes go live:
`sf community publish --name "FIMBY" 2>&1 | Select-Object -Last 20`

Use `working_directory: c:\Users\srathjen\FIMBY\FIMBY`. This applies to any deploy that includes one or more LWC bundles. Skip only if the user explicitly says not to publish.

**Publishing is asynchronous — wait before any live check.** The command only *queues* the publish ("We're publishing your changes now…"). It takes about **4 minutes** from queueing until the site is actually live (when Salesforce's confirmation email arrives). Until then the site serves the **old build**, so live results are meaningless.

- Note the time the publish was queued. Do **not** start browser QA, launch a browser/QA subagent, or tell the user the change is live until **at least 4 minutes** have passed.
- Commit + push can happen during the wait. Use the wait timer (e.g. `AwaitShell`), not a shell `sleep`.
- When the live check starts, first confirm the **new build** is being served: hard-reload and probe the DOM for a marker of the change. If it's still the old build, wait about 60s and reload; repeat a few times before reporting the publish as not yet live.

### Post-deploy: Git commit (mandatory — no prompt)

After **each successful** org deploy — and after community publish when the deploy included LWC — **commit immediately**. Do not ask “should I commit?” Deploy success is the trigger.

**Skip commit only when:**
- The deploy failed (including real test failures — not the locale `Finalizing` artifact)
- The user said keep local / deploy only / no commit / don’t commit in that message or thread
- `git commit` would be empty (nothing staged)

**Per deploy call (not end-of-session batch):**
1. Stage only paths that were part of **that** deploy (`--source-dir` / `--metadata` set), plus any net-new untracked files under those paths (whole LWC bundle folders, not single files).
2. If the same session changed related files not in the deploy path but required for the deployed feature (e.g. wiring in `fimbyUniversalHeader`), include those too — still scoped to the task, never the whole `force-app`.
3. Commit with a short **why** message, e.g. `Deploy: guided tour mobile bottom-nav lift fix` — not a file list.
4. **Push immediately** after the commit: `git push origin <current-branch>` (normally `main`) so every commit is backed up to GitHub with zero lag, not left local-only. This applies to **every** commit you create, not just deploy commits. Safety guards stay: never `--force`, never force-push to `main`, skip the push if the user said keep-local / deploy-only / no-commit. (A daily 9 AM scheduled task, "FIMBY Auto Git Sync" → `C:\Users\srathjen\FIMBY-automation\fimby-auto-sync.ps1`, still runs as a catch-all safety net that commits any uncommitted working files and pushes — but do not rely on it for timely backup of your own commits.)
5. **Never** stage secrets (`.env`, credentials).

Use a HEREDOC for the commit message. If a pre-commit hook fails, fix and create a **new** commit (do not amend unless amend rules apply).

This keeps git history aligned with what is live in the org and makes rollback a revert/checkout, not archaeology in untracked files.

CLI deploys LWC bundles, but not Experience Cloud pages or routes. If a deploy created or changed any of these, add an `Experience Cloud Setup Required` section at the end of the session summary:
- new page-level LWCs needing routes, like `fimbyManageIdentities` → `/manage-identities`
- new or changed route paths referenced by deployed navigation
- components needing page-level config, like property bindings or `recordId` from URL

Include it alongside the manual profile updates list. If no Experience Cloud updates are needed, omit this section.

### Custom Metadata Type records

`force-app/main/default/customMetadata/*.md-meta.xml` files are CMDT **records**, deployed via `--source-dir "force-app/main/default/customMetadata"` or by targeting the specific file. They deploy fine WITHOUT `--tests`. New record types (`force-app/main/default/objects/*__mdt/`) must be deployed BEFORE their records, or the record deploy fails with "Custom metadata type is not available in this organization."

The community user profile needs the **View Setup and Configuration** permission (or "Customize Application") to call `CustomMetadataType.getAll()` and `getInstance()` from Apex. If `FimbySettings.getUrl()` and `FimbyPublicWebsiteLinks.getUrl()` return blank in test runs but work in admin runs, this profile permission is the cause. The Cursor IDE browser MCP confirms it by checking the profile's System Permissions.

### Atomic deploy rollback (Apex + new fields)

A deploy is atomic per `sf project deploy start` call — if any test fails (including the synthetic "FAILED — coverage below 75%" warning), the ENTIRE deploy rolls back, including newly created custom fields/objects. Workaround: deploy schema-only changes (custom fields, picklist values, new CMDT types) in a separate call WITHOUT `--tests`, then deploy the Apex that depends on them in a second call WITH `--tests`. This is especially important for notification-pattern work where a new Apex class often references brand-new fields like `Vouch_Record__c.Last_Reminder_Sent_Date__c`.

